# TD-SEC-024 (see technical-debt-register.md for full detail): 7 HIGH-severity CVEs in the Go
# standard library Infisical's own CLI binary (ADR-0014) was compiled against (Go 1.25.12) —
# baked in at Infisical's own upstream build time, not something this project's own code
# introduces. Confirmed live (2026-08-24) that v0.43.125 is Infisical CLI's latest release and no
# newer build compiled against a patched Go toolchain (1.25.13/1.26.6/1.27.0-rc.3) exists yet —
# this is a real "vendor hasn't shipped a fix" gap, not something `apt-get install` a different
# version would resolve today.
#
# Every one of the 7 is a DoS/parsing-confusion class vulnerability reachable only by acting as
# a network server accepting untrusted connections, or by a malicious counterparty during a
# network exchange the vulnerable code initiates (a hostile TLS server, a hostile HTTP/2 peer, an
# XML/ASN.1 document from an untrusted source, HTML-template rendering of untrusted input). This
# binary's own real usage in this image (docker-entrypoint.sh) never does any of that: it runs
# exactly twice per container start (`infisical login`, `infisical run`), makes outbound HTTPS
# calls only, to the operator's own INFISICAL_DOMAIN — always the self-hosted `infisical` service
# in docker-compose.infisical.yml on this project's own Docker network, structurally never a
# third-party/attacker-supplied host, the same trust boundary already extended to `postgres`/
# `redis`. Never listens on a port, never parses XML, never renders an HTML template.
#
# Revisit (remove from this file, don't just re-add) the next time `apt-cache policy infisical`
# shows a newer version than 0.43.125 — check whether that build carries a patched Go toolchain
# before assuming the CVEs are gone.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
